/-! Data of the bitset certificate for the root-eight binary forest.

The 36 roots are one point of each orbit of the group generated by the four root-eight
letters on the singular binary masks: for the 23 type-four orbits a point nearest to Ω under
the ten odd source letters, and the least mask of each of the 13 remaining orbits (short classes
and zero). The 26 doubling steps are words in the four letters together with row operations
computing the binary matrix of each word. All data are discovery outputs; the kernel checks
every use. -/

@[expose] public section
namespace FormalizedTextbooks.FrenkelLepowskyMeurmanMonster

/-- The 23 type-four roots, one per orbit; the first is Ω. -/
def rootEightForestTypeFourRoots : List ℕ := [
    2048, 2304, 985102, 5181440, 3148544, 4201216, 5183502, 919566, 4200704, 6295808, 28680, 854030,
    4130828, 3147790, 4245504, 4243456, 4194574, 4612096, 4917248, 4766464, 4196352, 1574924,
    7340036]

/-- The roots of the 13 remaining singular orbits (zero and short classes). -/
def rootEightForestOtherRoots : List ℕ := [
    0, 3, 6, 7, 31, 32, 64, 92, 193, 5902, 17674, 327692, 6162432]

/-- All 36 roots. -/
def rootEightForestRoots : List ℕ := rootEightForestTypeFourRoots ++ rootEightForestOtherRoots

/-- The start set of the doubling: the roots. -/
def rootEightForestStart : ℕ := tenthForestOfList rootEightForestRoots

